######## ATTADIPA PEDOMETER PROBE ########
Writes CTRL2/CTRL7/CTRL8/CTRL9 and CAL1..CAL4 on the IMU at 0x6B.
Nothing else, on any device. No PMU write, no rail change, no display.

WHO_AM_I  = 0x05   (0x05 in both candidate datasheets)
REVISION  = 0x7C   (0x7C = QMI8658A 13-52-25 Rev A; 0x79 = QMI8658C Rev 0.6)

--- before ---   CTRL2=0x27 CTRL7=0x01 CTRL8=0x90

CTRL7 = 0x00 (aEN=gEN=0, required by 11.2 before configuring) -> ACK
CTRL8 = 0x80 (CTRL9 handshake on STATUSINT, Pedo_EN still 0)  -> ACK
CTRL2 = 0x16 (+/-8 g, 62.5 Hz accel-only)                     -> ACK
CTRL3 = 0x36 (+/-1000 dps, 112.1 Hz -- 6DOF needs the gyro up)  -> ACK

two CTRL9 0x0D calls (Table 38): both acknowledged -- CmdDone set and cleared each time
  sample_cnt=50  peak2peak=0x0050  peak=0x003C  time_up=400
  time_low=8  cnt_entry=1  precision=0  sig_count=1

CTRL8 = 0x90 (Pedo_EN; the 0->1 edge clears the count, 11.6) -> ACK
CTRL7 = 0x03 (aEN; the engine starts counting here, 11.3)     -> ACK
CTRL9 0x0F (reset step count): acknowledged
--- armed  ---   CTRL2=0x16 CTRL7=0x03 CTRL8=0x90  step count = 0

CTRL8 readback: accepted -- the register is writable, which the C Rev 0.6
  document does not describe (it calls CTRL8 Reserved: Not Used)

WHAT TO EXPECT, written down before the run so it cannot be fitted
afterwards. This is SensorLib's bring-up profile, not the datasheet's:
entry_count=1 and sig_count=1, so the register moves on the FIRST step
and on every step after it. No nine held back, no counting in fours.
Shaking the board in a walking rhythm should therefore make the count
climb roughly one per shake, visibly, within a few seconds. A count
that climbs at all -- by any amount, at any rate -- is the engine
working. A steady 0 while the p2p column reads OVER for many seconds
in a row is the engine not counting, and this time that is not
ambiguous, because the threshold it is being held to is printed next
to the motion it was given.
STATUS1 bit 4 is the pedometer event (11.4); it should stop being 0.

p2p is peak-to-peak per axis over each second, in mg. The engine's
threshold is ped_fix_peak2peak = 200 mg; ped_fix_peak = 100 mg is
measured against the running average, which this cannot see.

